{"causes": ["The succession of Hugh II, Peter III's father, left the Judicate of Arborea in a delicate balance of independence and Aragonese suzerainty.", "The ongoing expansionist ambitions of the Crown of Aragon exerted continuous pressure on the remaining independent Sardinian states.", "The intricate system of feudal allegiances and rivalries among Sardinian noble families and external powers created a complex political environment."], "effects": ["Peter III's reign ensured the continued, albeit fragile, independence of the Judicate of Arborea from Aragonese direct rule for over a decade.", "His diplomatic efforts and internal consolidation provided a stable foundation for the more aggressive anti-Aragonese policies of his successor, Marianus IV.", "The persistent Aragonese claims over Arborea during his rule contributed to a prolonged period of conflict in Sardinia that lasted for decades."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "hugh-ii-of-arborea", "sourceName": "Hugh II of Arborea", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "peter-iii-of-arborea", "targetName": "Peter III of Arborea", "context": "Peter III of Arborea assumed the Judicate upon the death of his father, Hugh II, in 1335 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "peter-iii-of-arborea", "sourceName": "Peter III of Arborea", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "sardinia", "targetName": "Sardinia", "context": "Peter III's entire reign as Judge of Arborea occurred on the island of Sardinia, which was a contested territory in the 14th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "crown-of-aragon", "sourceName": "Crown of Aragon", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "peter-iii-of-arborea", "targetName": "Peter III of Arborea", "context": "The expansionist policies and suzerainty claims of the Crown of Aragon heavily influenced Peter III's diplomatic and internal governance strategies."}, {"sourceSlug": "peter-iii-of-arborea", "sourceName": "Peter III of Arborea", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "marianus-iv-of-arborea", "targetName": "Marianus IV of